<title>SWEDEN: SAS adds two Saab 2000 on Swedish routes.</title>
<headline>SAS adds two Saab 2000 on Swedish routes.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scandinavian Airlines (SAS) said on Wednesday it will strenghten its Swedish traffic by adding two new Saab 2000 planes from February next year.</p>
<p>The two 47-seat planes, mean new departures for several destinations, more attractive departure times during peak time on a large part of domestic routes and more non-stop connections to and from Stockholm, SAS said.</p>
<p>The planes will run between Stockholm and Skelleftea, Stockholm-Kalmar and Stockholm-Ronneby.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001006</p>
</text>
